{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b20-ca21-764a-96a1-8edbc612c42f","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/skills/built-in/contracts/SKILL.md","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\neployed contract into `/home/user/app/src/App.tsx` (boilerplate in `references/contract-deploy.md`).\\n   246\\t- Everything else — including \\\"create/build/deploy a token/NFT/contract\\\" with no UI ask → do NOT touch `App.tsx`. Confirm the deploy in one short sentence and mention the artifact and metadata paths, then stop. Do NOT restate the raw address, tx hash, or explorer URL in prose — the chat timeline renders a contract card with all three from the deploy_contract result, and the Workbench's Contracts panel surfaces the deployment. If a UI would help, OFFER it in one sentence — never build one unprompted \\\"to be helpful\\\".\\n   247\\t\\n   248\\t## Hard rules (re-read before every contract action)\\n   249\\t\\n   250\\t- Default to a balanced review; never ask which review level to use. The only mid-thread questions allowed are the re-engagement points in \\\"Surfacing a finding or tradeoff\\\". This governs the review level and mid-flow interruptions only — it does NOT suppress the up-front requirements clarification that runs before STEP 1 when your mode calls for it (see \\\"Before STEP 1\\\" above).\\n   251\\t- Call it a \\\"review\\\", never an \\\"audit\\\", in everything the user sees.\\n   252\\t- The five subagents are siblings — never ask any of them to call `task()` (they have no subagents). Auditors are read-only; testers are read-only on contract source (they author test files only).\\n   253\\t- Always pass `severity level: <quick|balanced|max>` in every auditor `task()` description.\\n   254\\t- Always dispatch both auditors in the SAME assistant turn.\\n   255\\t- Never tell the user an auditor ran, or report its `## Audit Provenance` row, unless you actually dispatched it via `task(subagent_type=...)` in this turn and read that row back from its own report.\\n   256\\t- The audit-level severity governs ONLY the audit's tier and round-cap — it does NOT auto-trigger Slither or unit tests (those are gated by the preset's tool slots). Integration tests are never auto-run by any preset.\\n   257\\t- Never auto-run POST-deploy integration tests (STEP 8, Mode 1 / plain Mode 2). After a successful deploy, offer them in one sentence and run only if the user accepts. STEP 6's pre-deploy VERIFY-ON-FORK gate (Compass-engine Mode 2) is the one exception — it always runs, in every preset, and is not an offer.\\n   258\\t- Never pass `--mode live` to `compass:deploy` unless STEP 6's gate ran and passed this session. Otherwise omit `--mode` and let `fork-then-live` rehearse — and know that rehearsal is a single constructor run, not STEP 6's integration tests (see STEP 7).\\n   259\\t- Initial writes always go to `contract-writer`. Big rewrites and multi-finding fixes also go to the writer.\\n   260\\t- Always read `references/contract-deploy.md` in full before any deploy (and the matching mode file in full once you've picked a mode); read `references/static-analysis.md` in full before running Slither.\\n   261\\t- Always run STEP 3a (preview) before STEP 3b (apply).\\n   262\\t- Never silently move past unresolved Critical / High findings, unresolved Slither findings, unresolved test failures, or unresolved live-behaviour discrepancies.\\n   263\\t- \\\"Deploy it anyway\\\" and any equivalent phrase is NOT consent to fix + deploy. When the user expresses deploy intent alongside an unresolved Critical/High finding, surface the binary choice per \\\"Surfacing a finding or tradeoff\\\" (deploy as-is with known risk, OR fix first then deploy) and wait for explicit selection. Never choose either path autonomously.\\n   264\\t- Stay on balanced unless an unambiguous keyword switches to quick or max.\\n   265\\t- Never build a frontend/UI unless the original request explicitly asked for an app/UI/page/demo — contract + deploy is the default deliverable. Do not infer UI intent from \\\"create/build a token/contract\\\".\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_014LLgbk1HdGDxEtFdiWG9dx\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a17b20-ca1f-731f-8719-8a155c3c51d0","toolName":"read_file","args":{"file_path":"/home/user/app/context/phase1/spec/ShiftProof-interface.md","limit":2000},"result":"... (truncated)\ncontract against §5 and §10 without the author’s context.\\n   375\\t\\n   376\\t### 10.2 What “secure” does not mean here\\n   377\\t\\n   378\\t\\n   379\\t### 14.2 Unit test cases\\n   380\\t\\n   381\\t| ID | Test | Expected |\\n   382\\t|---|---|---|\\n   383\\t| U01 | Create with valid worker/rate/duration | `ShiftCreated`; escrow pulled; `nextShiftId` increments |\\n   384\\t| U02 | Create with zero worker | `ZeroAddress`/`InvalidWorker` |\\n   385\\t| U03 | Create with worker == employer | `InvalidWorker` |\\n   386\\t| U04 | Create with zero rate | `InvalidAmount` |\\n   387\\t| U05 | Create with zero duration | `InvalidDuration` |\\n   388\\t| U06 | Create with duration > 24h | `DurationTooLong` |\\n   389\\t| U07 | Create with escrow > 10,000 USDC | `EscrowTooLarge` |\\n   390\\t| U08 | Create with insufficient allowance/balance | USDC revert; no shift |\\n   391\\t| U09 | Create with a 6-decimal mock | Works |\\n   392\\t| U10 | Create with an 18-decimal token | `InvalidDecimals` |\\n   393\\t| U11 | Clock in by worker | `Active`; `startedAt` set |\\n   394\\t| U12 | Clock in by non-worker | `NotWorker` |\\n   395\\t| U13 | Clock in twice | `InvalidStatus` |\\n   396\\t| U14 | Clock out by worker | `AwaitingAttestation`; `endedAt` set |\\n   397\\t| U15 | Clock out before clock-in | `InvalidStatus` |\\n   398\\t| U16 | Clock in and out in the same block | Allowed; `endedAt == startedAt` |\\n   399\\t| U17 | Attest by employer | `Attested`; `owed` correct; no USDC movement |\\n   400\\t| U18 | Attest by non-employer | `NotEmployer` |\\n   401\\t| U19 | Attest seconds > max | `AttestedTooLong` |\\n   402\\t| U20 | Attest 0 | `Attested`; `owed = 0` |\\n   403\\t| U21 | Attest full | `owed = escrow` |\\n   404\\t| U22 | Attest from `Funded` (timer skip) | `Attested`; `endedAt` set |\\n   405\\t| U23 | Attest from `Active` | `Attested`; `endedAt` set |\\n   406\\t| U24 | Claim by worker | USDC to worker; `Claimed`/`Settled` |\\n   407\\t| U25 | Claim by non-worker | `NotWorker` |\\n   408\\t| U26 | Claim twice | `InvalidStatus` |\\n   409\\t| U27 | Claim with zero owed | `NothingToClaim` |\\n   410\\t| U28 | Refund unused by anyone | USDC to employer; escrow reduced |\\n   411\\t| U29 | Refund before attest | `InvalidStatus` |\\n   412\\t| U30 | Refund twice | `NothingToRefund` |\\n   413\\t| U31 | Refund after claim | Residual to employer; `Settled` |\\n   414\\t| U32 | Cancel by employer in `Funded` | Full refund; `Cancelled` |\\n   415\\t| U33 | Cancel by non-employer | `NotEmployer` |\\n   416\\t| U34 | Cancel after clock-in | `InvalidStatus` |\\n   417\\t| U35 | Cancel twice | `InvalidStatus` |\\n   418\\t| U36 | Read nonexistent shift | `None`/zero fields |\\n   419\\t| U37 | `getShifts` with >50 IDs | `TooManyIds` |\\n   420\\t| U38 | Direct USDC donation | Balance increases; `totalEscrow` unchanged; no sweep |\\n   421\\t| U39 | Reentrant mock token | `nonReentrant` blocks; no double spend |\\n   422\\t| U40 | Event arguments/indexing | Match ABI |\\n   423\\t\\n   424\\t### 14.3 Fuzz and invariant tests\\n   425\\t\\n   426\\t**Fuzz:**\\n   427\\t\\n   428\\t- `hourlyRate` uniform in `[1, 1_000e6]`.\\n   429\\t- `maxSeconds` uniform in `[1, 86_400]`.\\n   430\\t- `attestedSeconds` uniform in `[0, maxSeconds]`.\\n   431\\t- Random actor for each call; expected revert only for documented guards.\\n   432\\t- Assert `owed <= escrow`, `escrow <= maxEscrow`, `totalEscrow` reflects the sum.\\n   433\\t\\n   434\\t**Invariant handler:**\\n   435\\t\\n   436\\t- `create`, `clockIn`, `clockOut`, `attest`, `claim`, `refundUnused`, `cancel` with bounded random inputs and actors.\\n   437\\t- After each sequence: contract balance ≥ `totalEscrow`; no shift’s escrow increased; no double claim; terminal states reject writes; `totalEscrow` equals the sum.\\n   438\\t- Seed with a few hand-written sequences to ensure coverage.\\n   439\\t\\n   440\\t### 14.4 Fork and integration tests\"}],\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01MFAycget4NkDM6JKvevVrS\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"metadata\":{\"versions\":{\"@langchain/core\":\"1.2.18\"}},\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}"}}
